issue_context.body:
## 🚀 Feature Proposal

I propose we call `reply.send()` in synchronous routes if the returned value is not Promise or a Stream.

## Motivation

It seems a lot of newbies to fastify mistake the use of `async`, and we are not providing them a good developer experience.

## Example

```js
'use strict';

module.exports = (server, opts, done) => {

  server.get('/', () => {
    return "Hello World";
  });

  done();
};
```

comments:
I've seen this happening so many times that is pretty clear that newbie JS developers do not understand the critical differences between `async function` and `function`. This issue originates from that request. I'm not going to do a survey because the sample for that survey are going to be totally skewed.

I'm happy to make Fastify return a 500 and an error in that case. Practically, we should change these three lines: https://github.com/fastify/fastify/blob/7fa4bddca07aac18e0600cff40d97b95a96ab970/lib/handleRequest.js#L112-L114.
Making it return would change that block to:

```js
  var result = reply.context.handler(request, reply)
  if (result) {
    if (typeof result.then === 'function') {
      wrapThenable(result, reply)
    } else {
      reply.send(new Error('return a promise or use an async function in the route handler'))
      // or reply.send(result)
    }
  }
```

I think this change should be part of v3.
